//
// Expected: c0a1a1 at one session and at two — a message crossing four
// principals, end-to-end authenticated only on the last hop. Every
// intermediary forwards without checking anything, so the authentication
// query asked at an unchecked hop fails. The one asked where the MAC is
// verified fails too, because HopTwo can be bypassed: at one session the
// attacker replaces body at HopOne with nil, so HopTwo forwards nil, and
// hands Dana the body it observed on Alice's send. Dana's checks pass on a
// body HopTwo never sent. The judge once excused a delivered value equal to
// the honest one when the sender had not sent it, and pinned a0 there.
//
// Four hops is the point: attacker knowledge, provenance and the wire metadata
// on each slot all have to survive being copied from principal to principal
// several times. `known_by` is a list of (recipient, sender) pairs and
// `mutatable_to` a set of recipients, and a chain this long is where a
// single-sender or single-recipient simplification of either would start
// reporting the wrong provenance — most likely by attributing the message to
// the first hop rather than to whoever actually put it on the wire.
// The nonce on `n_body` is declared rather than generated so the ciphertext
// stays the same value in every session. At two sessions the attacker
// replaces body at HopOne with nil, so HopTwo forwards nil to Dana, and
// delivers Dana the body HopTwo#2 sends in its place. Dana and Dana#2 both
// pass their checks on a body HopTwo sent once: duplicate acceptance, as in
// auth_withheld_static_replay.vp with the sender diverted rather than
// halted. The search once never restored an honest input at a recipient
// that a tampered upstream run had made halt, and in some declaration orders
// the executor delivered an install before its sender sent the same value,
// marking HopTwo's forwarded copy attacker-authored and reporting a duplicate
// for the wrong reason.

attacker[active]

principal Alice[
	knows private mac_key
	knows private m
	knows private seal_key
	knows private n_body
	body = AEAD_ENC(seal_key, n_body, m, nil)
	tag = MAC(mac_key, body)
]

Alice -> HopOne: n_body, body, tag

principal HopOne[
	_ = HASH(body, tag)
]

HopOne -> HopTwo: n_body, body, tag

principal HopTwo[
	_ = HASH(body, tag)
]

HopTwo -> Dana: n_body, body, tag

principal Dana[
	knows private mac_key
	knows private seal_key
	_ = ASSERT(MAC(mac_key, body), tag)?
	got = AEAD_DEC(seal_key, n_body, body, nil)?
	_ = HASH(got)
]

queries[
	confidentiality? m
	authentication? Alice -> HopOne: body
	authentication? HopTwo -> Dana: body
]
